addresses.comment:
**Lua `minister:PrioritizeBuildQueue()`**, which ProductionMinister_Tick calls when `math.mod(CCurrentGameState.GetAIRand(), 7) == 0`. Moves lines to the front of the queue; reorders nothing else:

    for line in country->Constructions (+0xF40), head to tail:
        if line->status (+0x3C) >= (int)floor(980.5f) = 980: continue      ; got 98% of a day or more
        if line is a convoy (slot 15):
            if line->escort (+0x58): continue
            if country->Transports (+0xB0) * 2 < country->TotalNeededTransports (+0xB8):
                post CChangePriorityCommand(tag, line->id, -2)
        else if this->Desperation (+0x5C) > 0.6f and line is military (slot 17)
                and line->Brigades (+0x7C) first ->Type->is_land (+0x2D):
            days = status == 0 ? -1 : (duration (+0x34) - progress (+0x38)) * 1000 / status
            if days / 1000 < 120: post CChangePriorityCommand(tag, line->id, -2)

-2 is 'unlink and push on the front' (CChangePriorityCommand::Execute). The commands go through the in-game screen's session and run later, in the order posted, so **the lines moved end up at the front in reverse order** and nothing moves while the walk is going. Building lines are never moved. See reversing/findings/FINDINGS-ministers.md, section B.
